# EVL-105 authorized CPU pair

Use the exact approved Qwen3-0.6B files and cached vLLM 0.29.0 CPU image
from the retained direct run. Keep the original direct request bytes and
pin the same engine configuration, including engine seed 42, float32,
no prefix caching and the original greedy requests. The backend is served
under two names for the same model path. The admitted gateway name is
first so that the backend response meets the gateway's strict model check.

The vLLM request decoder preserves the caller's seed and temperature. Its
sampling parameter logic selects greedy before inspecting the seed. The
CPU runner's V2 sampler calls the Triton Gumbel kernel. Its zero-temperature
branch selects argmax without generating Gumbel noise. Preserve the vLLM
source files from the exact cached image and verify both cases against the
original direct digests. The tracked gateway injects the same disabled
thinking flag into tokenization and generation. A nonzero temperature,
changed model or changed template would require a separate qualification.

Use the repository's existing real gateway distribution fixture with the
signed fixture license, issued test credentials and scoped published alias.
The fixture retains synthetic deployment and GPU observations for admission.
A bounded loopback bridge forwards the gateway body unchanged to real vLLM
and records it. The bridge does not insert a seed or synthesize a reply.
Use two exact direct calls and two serial gateway calls. Match request
inputs, the backend and public completion IDs, output text digests, finish
reason and token usage. Join the server gateway ID to its actual scoped
PostgreSQL admission and the HTTPS acknowledgment, recompute its canonical
digest and check released capacity and one report audit. This proves an
authenticated acknowledgment and not a detached cryptographic signature.

The reused dependency and model licenses are recorded in the EVL-105
research. The harness adds no dependency, data or product artifact. Use
only the previously approved cached images and synthetic fixture prompts.
PostgreSQL owns a network-none namespace. The model and test join only
that namespace and publish no host ports. Remove only this run's resources.
